391 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 117 0 R/T(From competitors analysis, we have built two competitive positioning maps. For the e-commerce map, we have chosen the variables \217distributative coverage\220 and \217heagenic product offering\220. The first variable is useful to get an overview of distribution coverage in the various countries. The second variable allows you to identify the type of products available, i.e. whether the shop has a variety of products specific and / or exclusive to the brand or heterogenic. For the map compared to the physical shop, we have chosen the variables \217strategic location of the shop\220 and \217New York\220s \217souvenir\220 product offer\220. The first variable concerns the geographical visibility of the physical shop. The second variable is, on the other hand, understood as the possibility of buying a product that can act as a souvenir and, therefore, as a unique memory of the city of New York.)/E(From competitors analysis, we have built two competitive positioning maps. For the e-commerce map, we have chosen the variables \217distributative coverage\220 and \217heagenic product offering\220. The first variable is useful to get an overview of distribution coverage in the various countries. The second variable allows you to identify the type of products available, i.e. whether the shop has a variety of products specific and / or exclusive to the brand or heterogenic. For the map compared to the physical shop, we have chosen the variables \217strategic location of the shop\220 and \217New York\220s \217souvenir\220 product offer\220. The first variable concerns the geographical visibility of the physical shop. The second variable is, on the other hand, understood as the possibility of buying a product that can act as a souvenir and, therefore, as a unique memory of the city of New York.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

