endobj

501 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 120 0 R/E(W = age of the target \(their target is mainly made up of adults and groupings, above all, the category between 15-35 years old\); organizational structure \(NBC's organizational structure is compatible with their current business model: it has limitations regarding expansion into different market segments\); keep up with the changing Trends \(being an international mass media company, they have to adjust their behaviors according to the local market where it should\); depends too much on advertising.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

502 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 120 0 R/E(O = new markets \(this is a huge opportunity for NBC, as there are always new markets opening up\); growing economy \(the growing economy brings new customers to NBC. The latter can be acquired thanks to a good strategy\); international growth \(as a multinational company, NBC is constantly looking for new markets to grow internationally. For example, they have a huge stake in India and Latin America\).)/Pg 28 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

