endobj

623 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E( Early 70s setting. Everything is in black and white. Ateenager lives in a traditional, very protective family that suffocates his ambitions. Until one day he sees a crowd of protesters \(a reference to the counterculture\), who are the only ones to be colored and from there he is so impressed that he wants to be part of it \(also he becomes colored\). After that the scene changes and on his way home he sits down and turns on the TV where the colored peacock appears and the parents stop to look at him curiously. Finally, the title "Brought to you living color" appears.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

624 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(EPISODIO DUE: "Embracing Change" )/Pg 35 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

625 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 127 0 R/E(The teenage boy has grown up \(although he should be 60 I would leave him quite young up to 40\) and now he lives in New York here he has his life. On his way back from work he stops in a bar where he meets a black woman. While they are talking, she takes an alcoholic drink and he doesn't \(this is how the change is referred to, because according to the stereotype the man takes alcoholic drinks more often and the woman doesn't\) they get to know each other and decide to meet again at the girl's house and when they turn on the TV the peacock appears with the writing embracing change.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

626 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 127 0 R/T(EPISODIO TRE: "Back to the future" A few years after their meeting they live together and while they are at home they decide to go for a walk. They pass through Times Square and while they are there an NBC advertisement passes where they review their life made up of the past up to a future with children, there are also couple scenes as if it were an advertisement for an American series. So after all that they go away happy and there is the writing #makethehistory with us.)/E(EPISODIO TRE: "Back to the future" A few years after their meeting they live together and while they are at home they decide to go for a walk. They pass through Times Square and while they are there an NBC advertisement passes where they review their life made up of the past up to a future with children, there are also couple scenes as if it were an advertisement for an American series. So after all that they go away happy and there is the writing #makethehistory with us.)/Pg 35 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

